Reference programs and data
- FullProf Suite (J. Rodríguez-Carvajal, Institut Laue-Langevin) and GSAS-II (B. H. Toby, R. B. Von Dreele, Argonne
  National Laboratory) are the references the core's results are checked against; neither is distributed here.
- The Tb2Pd2Sn patterns shown in the guide come from the WinPLOTR tutorial of the FullProf Suite (T. Roisnel,
  J. Rodríguez-Carvajal); they are not distributed here.
- The example heating run is synthetic, computed by the diff-ref-struct core.

How it was made
diff-ref-struct and diff-ref-struct Web are written with AI assistance: Claude (Anthropic), used through Claude Code,
writes code and documents under the direction of Josu M. Igartua, who sets the requirements, reads the results and
decides every change. Nothing is accepted on the assistant's word: every number the tool shows is computed by the core
and checked by its tests against reference programs and published data, and every change is recorded in the project's
log with its evidence. The responsibility for the tool and its results is the author's.
